  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Dry and cool conditions early this week.\nTemperatures gradually warm to seasonable values by Wednesday.\n\nA widespread freeze occurred across Southeast South Carolina \nand Southeast Georgia this morning. The National Weather Service\nin Charleston has discontinued Frost Advisories and Freeze \nWatches/Warnings until March 1st of next year.\n\nNudged lows down a degree or two for many areas per near term\nmodel trends.\n\nHigh pressure will provide dry conditions with a weak pressure \ngradient this evening into tonight. Another night of light to \ncalm winds with mostly clear sky conditions, providing hours of \nnearly ideal radiational cooling conditions. Low temperatures \nare forecast to range from the low to mid 30s inland to the 40s \nalong the coast.\n\nLarge sfc high pressure is forecast to remain across the region\nthrough most of this week. Temperatures should gradually modify\neach day, warming to near normals, around 70 degrees, by\nWednesday. \n\nThe forecast will feature no mentionable PoPs over land this\nweek.",
